# Screenshot captures — 840 full-page PNGs, 400MB (measured 2026-08-29:
# 840 files, 400,472,802 bytes). One per required route, matching this set's own
# committed `docs/screenshots/manifest.json`, which records capturedRoutes 840 and
# carries 840 rows. The MANIFEST is committed and the images are not: the manifest
# is the deliverable that must be reviewable in a diff, and 400MB of binary is not
# something a repository should carry to describe pages it already describes in text.
#
# This comment used to say "85 PNGs, 173MB, regenerated by `pnpm screenshots` in
# about ninety seconds." All three were false: the count was off by ~10x, the size
# by more than 2x, and there is NO `pnpm screenshots` script — it was deleted with
# the test suites under APP-020, as `docs/screenshots/README.md` has said all along.
# So these are not cheap to rebuild either; there is no command that rebuilds them.
# What makes excluding them survivable is the committed manifest, not a rebuild.
docs/screenshots/*.png
# Live-verification captures. NOT the same reasoning as the rule above, and the
# line that said it was is corrected here (unit-01 final whole-branch review,
# IMPORTANT 4). Neither set is reproducible any more, so the difference is not
# rebuild cost — it is WHAT VOUCHES for the bytes. The set above is described
# route-by-route by a committed manifest. These are a manual browser-driving
# session against a served export, following
# `docs/process/live-verification-procedure.md`, that no script reproduces and no
# manifest enumerates. Lose them and the evidence is gone for good.
#
# They are still excluded, because 148MB of PNG (measured 2026-08-29 against this
# rule's own glob: 247 files, 147,844,581 bytes — the 134MB this line first claimed
# was `du` on ONE subdirectory, and read a MiB figure as MB) is not what a history should
# carry, and because this project's own deny rules stop an agent reading an image
# back anyway. What makes the exclusion survivable is the ATTESTATION, not the
# rebuild: every path a ledger row cites carries a `sha256` beside it in
# `docs/process/ledgers/live-verification-ledger.json`, the same pattern both
# manifests use, so a reference stays checkable against bytes that travel
# separately. Irreproducible is an argument FOR hashing them, never for treating
# them as regenerable furniture.
#
# Step 7 of the procedure writes here so the Playwright MCP server stops
# defaulting to the repository's PARENT directory.
docs/screenshots/live/**/*.png
